  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6609.04 Denying Exception or Exemption",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6609.04 Denying Exception or Exemption.\n\n(a) The commissioner shall deny a request for exception or exemption if the requestor does not demonstrate:\n\n(1) The need for an exception or exemption;\n\n(2) That the public health, safety and welfare will not be compromised; or\n\n(3) Any other reason that would be contrary to the intent of these rules and RSA 107-D.\n\nSource. #7287, eff 5-24-00; ss by #9154, eff 5-8-08\n\nAPPENDIX",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6600.html"
}
